/-!
# Candidate adapted coordinates for the natural induced Mathieu module

The columns extend the saved 15-dimensional basis through the saved
60-dimensional basis to the whole 66-dimensional field space. The matrices
use column vectors and field digits 0, 1, omega, 1 + omega, with coordinate
3*i+j. These definitions alone assert neither invertibility, invariance nor
simplicity. Separate certificates must establish those properties for the
actual induced action. Provenance and the reproducible generator are in
`source/README.md` and `source/generate.py`.

Source context: Guralnick–Malle, Classification of 2F-modules I,
Proposition 5.1, pp.15–16 and Theorem 6.6/Table 6.7.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace Sporadic.Mathieu.M22TripleCover.DegreeTwentyFour.ExclusionsTwelve.InducedCoordinates.NaturalFiltration

abbrev Field := Representation.SL3FourNaturalDual.F

/-- Read an F₄ digit, with omega in the high bit. -/
def digit (v : ℕ) (j : ℕ) : Field :=
  (if v.testBit (2*j) then 1 else 0) +
    (if v.testBit (2*j+1) then QuadraticAlgebra.omega else 0)

